t a completely random hand, and significantly less against a range that would justify such a large raise. Calling requires risking the entire stack on a "bad bet" (negative expected value).\n\nReason: To maximize the cumulative score and probability of winning the game, one must avoid calling large bets with low-equity hands. Calling here would result in a significant long-term loss of chips. Folding minimizes the loss to just the initial blind/bet, preserving the stack (and cumulative score) for hands with better winning probabilities.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
